---
import Layout from '../layouts/Layout.astro';
import { business } from '../config';

const updated = '17 November 2026';
---

<Layout
  title="Privacy Policy — Krause IT"
  description="How Krause IT collects, uses and protects personal information from website visitors, enquiries and clients."
>
  <section class="section">
    <div class="container prose">
      <span class="badge badge-brand">Privacy</span>
      <h1>Privacy policy</h1>
      <p class="prose-meta">Last updated {updated}</p>

      <p>
        {business.name} (ABN {business.abn}) builds and hosts websites for small businesses and community groups.
        This policy explains what personal information we collect through this website and when we work together,
        how we use it, and the choices you have. We aim to handle personal information in line with the Australian
        Privacy Principles.
      </p>

      <h2>What we collect</h2>
      <ul>
        <li><strong>When you send an enquiry:</strong> your name, email address, business or organisation name (if given), what you need, your message, and any options you selected in the quote builder.</li>
        <li><strong>When you become a client:</strong> the contact, billing and project details needed to build, host and support your website, including access details for your domain, hosting or website where you provide them.</li>
        <li><strong>When you browse this site:</strong> anonymous usage information collected by Google Analytics, described below.</li>
      </ul>
      <p>We don't ask for sensitive information, and we ask that you don't include it in your enquiry.</p>

      <h2>How we use it</h2>
      <ul>
        <li>To reply to your enquiry and prepare a quote.</li>
        <li>To deliver, host and support the services you've engaged us for, and to invoice for them.</li>
        <li>To understand how visitors use this website so we can improve it.</li>
      </ul>
      <p>We don't sell your information, rent it out, or use it for unrelated marketing.</p>

      <h2>Where it's stored and who we share it with</h2>
      <p>We use a small number of trusted service providers to run this website and our business:</p>
      <ul>
        <li><strong>Netlify</strong> hosts this website and receives contact form submissions. Netlify stores data on servers that may be located outside Australia, including in the United States.</li>
        <li><strong>Microsoft 365</strong> provides our email, including notifications of new enquiries.</li>
        <li><strong>Google Analytics</strong> measures website usage. Google may process this data outside Australia.</li>
      </ul>
      <p>
        These providers handle information on our behalf under their own privacy and security commitments.
        We only otherwise disclose personal information if you agree or if the law requires it.
      </p>

      <h2>Cookies and analytics</h2>
      <p>
        This website uses Google Analytics, which sets cookies to measure things like how many people visit,
        which pages they view and roughly where they're visiting from. It doesn't tell us who you are, and Google
        Analytics 4 does not store visitors' IP addresses. You can block or delete cookies in your browser settings,
        or opt out using Google's
        <a href="https://tools.google.com/dlpage/gaoptout" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Analytics opt-out browser add-on</a>.
        This site does not use advertising or remarketing cookies.
      </p>

      <h2>How long we keep it</h2>
      <p>
        We keep enquiries for as long as needed to respond and follow up. Client records are kept while we work
        together and afterwards for as long as required for tax and business record-keeping. When information is
        no longer needed, we delete it.
      </p>

      <h2>Keeping it secure</h2>
      <p>
        We take reasonable steps to protect personal information from misuse, loss and unauthorised access,
        including secure (HTTPS) connections, access controls and reputable service providers.
      </p>

      <h2>Accessing or correcting your information</h2>
      <p>
        You can ask for a copy of the personal information we hold about you, ask us to correct it, or ask us to
        delete it, by emailing <a href={`mailto:${business.email}`}>{business.email}</a>. We'll respond within a
        reasonable time.
      </p>

      <h2>Questions and complaints</h2>
      <p>
        If you have a question or concern about how we've handled your information, please email
        <a href={`mailto:${business.email}`}>{business.email}</a> and we'll do our best to resolve it.
        If you're not satisfied with our response, you can contact the
        <a href="https://www.oaic.gov.au/privacy/privacy-complaints" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Office of the Australian Information Commissioner (OAIC)</a>.
      </p>

      <h2>Changes to this policy</h2>
      <p>We may update this policy from time to time. The latest version will always be on this page.</p>
    </div>
  </section>
</Layout>

<style>
  .prose {
    max-width: 760px;
  }

  .prose h1 {
    margin: var(--spacing-sm) 0 var(--spacing-xs);
    font-size: clamp(2.25rem, 4vw, 3rem);
  }

  .prose-meta {
    font-size: 0.95rem;
    margin-bottom: var(--spacing-lg);
  }

  .prose h2 {
    font-size: 1.4rem;
    letter-spacing: normal;
    margin: var(--spacing-lg) 0 var(--spacing-sm);
  }

  .prose p,
  .prose li {
    font-size: 1.02rem;
    line-height: 1.7;
    color: var(--color-text-muted);
  }

  .prose p + p {
    margin-top: var(--spacing-sm);
  }

  .prose ul {
    display: flex;
    flex-direction: column;
    gap: 0.5rem;
    padding-left: 1.25rem;
    margin-bottom: var(--spacing-sm);
  }

  .prose strong {
    color: var(--color-text-main);
  }

  .prose a {
    color: var(--color-brand);
    text-decoration: underline;
    text-underline-offset: 2px;
  }
</style>
